Q: Change taskbar menu in Tauri A: <p>While Tauri still doesn't support the Windows Taskbar Thumbnail Toolbar directly, I have successfully added it to my project, <a href="https://github.com/HasibulHasan098/VYRA-MUSIC" rel="nofollow noreferrer">VYRA Music</a>, using an unofficial method with the <code>ITaskbarList3</code> COM interface.</p>
<h2>Working Implementation</h2>
<p>Here's how I accomplished it:</p>
<h3>1. Add Dependencies to <code>Cargo.toml</code></h3>
<pre class="lang-ini prettyprint-override"><code>[target.'cfg(windows)'.dependencies]
windows = { version = &quot;0.58&quot;, features = [
    &quot;Win32_UI_Shell&quot;,
    &quot;Win32_UI_WindowsAndMessaging&quot;,
    &quot;Win32_UI_Controls&quot;,
    &quot;Win32_Foundation&quot;,
    &quot;Win32_Graphics_Gdi&quot;,
    &quot;Win32_System_LibraryLoader&quot;,
    &quot;Win32_System_Com&quot;,
] }
image = &quot;0.25&quot;  # For loading PNG icons
</code></pre>
<h3>2. Implementation Overview</h3>
<pre class="lang-rust prettyprint-override"><code>#[cfg(target_os = &quot;windows&quot;)]
mod taskbar_buttons {
    use windows::Win32::UI::Shell::{ITaskbarList3, TaskbarList, THUMBBUTTON};
    use windows::Win32::System::Com::{CoCreateInstance, CoInitializeEx, CLSCTX_INPROC_SERVER, COINIT_APARTMENTTHREADED};

    // Button IDs
    pub const BTN_PREV: u32 = 0;
    pub const BTN_PLAY: u32 = 1;
    pub const BTN_NEXT: u32 = 2;

    pub fn init_taskbar_buttons(app_handle: AppHandle, hwnd: isize) {
        std::thread::spawn(move || {
            unsafe {
                CoInitializeEx(None, COINIT_APARTMENTTHREADED);

                let hwnd_win = HWND(hwnd as *mut std::ffi::c_void);

                // Create ITaskbarList3 instance
                let taskbar: ITaskbarList3 = CoCreateInstance(&amp;TaskbarList, None, CLSCTX_INPROC_SERVER).unwrap();
                taskbar.HrInit().unwrap();

                // Create buttons with icons
                let buttons = [
                    THUMBBUTTON {
                        dwMask: THB_FLAGS | THB_TOOLTIP | THB_ICON,
                        iId: BTN_PREV,
                        hIcon: create_icon_from_png(),
                        szTip: string_to_wide_array(&quot;Previous&quot;),
                        dwFlags: THBF_ENABLED,
                        // ...
                    },
                    // ... more buttons
                ];

                taskbar.ThumbBarAddButtons(hwnd_win, &amp;buttons);
            }
        });
    }

    // Update button dynamically
    pub fn update_button(hwnd: isize, button_id: u32, new_icon: HICON) {
        std::thread::spawn(move || {
            unsafe {
                CoInitializeEx(None, COINIT_APARTMENTTHREADED);
                let taskbar: ITaskbarList3 = CoCreateInstance(&amp;TaskbarList, None, CLSCTX_INPROC_SERVER).unwrap();
                taskbar.HrInit().unwrap();

                let button = THUMBBUTTON {
                    dwMask: THB_ICON | THB_FLAGS,
                    iId: button_id,
                    hIcon: new_icon,
                    dwFlags: THBF_ENABLED,
                    // ...
                };

                taskbar.ThumbBarUpdateButtons(HWND(hwnd as *mut _), &amp;[button]);
            }
        });
    }
}
</code></pre>
<h3>3. Handle Button Clicks</h3>
<p>Subclass the window to intercept <code>WM_COMMAND</code> messages:</p>
<pre class="lang-rust prettyprint-override"><code>unsafe extern &quot;system&quot; fn subclass_wndproc(hwnd: HWND, msg: u32, wparam: WPARAM, lparam: LPARAM) -&gt; LRESULT {
    if msg == WM_COMMAND {
        let hi_word = ((wparam.0 &gt;&gt; 16) &amp; 0xFFFF) as u32;
        let lo_word = (wparam.0 &amp; 0xFFFF) as u32;

        if hi_word == 0x1800 { // THBN_CLICKED
            // Handle button click based on lo_word (button ID)
            emit_to_frontend(lo_word);
        }
    }
    // Call original window procedure
}
</code></pre>
<h3>4. Initialize in Tauri Setup</h3>
<pre class="lang-rust prettyprint-override"><code>.setup(|app| {
    let app_handle = app.handle().clone();
    if let Some(window) = app.get_webview_window(&quot;main&quot;) {
        std::thread::spawn(move || {
            std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_millis(500));
            if let Ok(hwnd) = window.hwnd() {
                taskbar_buttons::init_taskbar_buttons(app_handle, hwnd.0 as isize);
            }
        });
    }
    Ok(())
})
</code></pre>
<h2>Key Features Achieved</h2>
<ul>
<li>Add buttons with custom icons (PNG embedded with <code>include_bytes!</code>)</li>
<li>Update buttons dynamically (e.g., play to pause)</li>
<li>Handle button clicks and send events to the frontend</li>
<li>Proper icon transparency with ARGB format</li>
</ul>
<h2>Full Implementation</h2>
<p>Check out the complete working code in [<a href="https://github.com/HasibulHasan098/VYRA-MUSIC/blob/main/src-tauri/src/main.rs" rel="nofollow noreferrer">VYRA Music source</a>](<a href="https://github.com/HasibulHasan098/VYRA-MUSIC/blob/main/src-tauri/src/main.rs" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://github.com/HasibulHasan098/VYRA-MUSIC/blob/main/src-tauri/src/main.rs</a>) (see the <code>taskbar_buttons</code> module around line 20-250).</p>
<h2>Notes</h2>
<ul>
<li>You need to create a new <code>ITaskbarList3</code> instance for each update because COM interfaces can't be stored in statics.</li>
<li>Icons should be 16x16 pixels for best results.</li>
<li>Use <code>CoInitializeEx</code> in each thread that uses COM.</li>
<li>The implementation works perfectly in production builds.</li>
</ul>
<p>Hope this helps! Let me know if you need more details on any specific part.</p>
